# Set ONE of these in Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables,
# then REDEPLOY. Env vars only take effect on a new deployment.
# WEBHOOK_URL wins if both are set.
#
# With neither set, submission shows a retry/copy fallback and no notification
# is delivered. The attempted answer is still visible in Vercel function logs.

# ---- Option A: ntfy (set up, no signup, lands on your phone) ----
# The topic IS the password. Anyone who knows the string can read the messages
# and post to it, so treat it like a secret and do not paste it anywhere public.
# The handler detects ntfy and sends a plain-text body, so the phone shows a
# readable message instead of raw JSON.
# The topic is a SECRET. Keep the real one in Vercel only, never in this file.
WEBHOOK_URL=https://ntfy.sh/CHANGE-ME-to-your-private-topic

# Also works, unchanged, if you would rather use these:
#   Discord   Server Settings -> Integrations -> Webhooks -> New -> Copy URL
#   Slack     https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks

# ---- Option B: email via Resend ----
RESEND_API_KEY=
NOTIFY_FROM=notify@yourdomain.tld
NOTIFY_TO=kish@nex.co.nz
